  [1mTwo problems the CSP test caught[0m
  - [1mAuth script:[0m Firebase Auth's default setup loaded a Google script for popup sign-in, which we
    don't use. I switched to email-link-only auth instead of allowing that host.
  - [1mInlined fonts:[0m Vite was embedding small fonts as [38;2;177;185;249mdata:[39m URIs. I stopped that instead of loosening
    [38;2;177;185;249mfont-src[39m.

  [1mWhat you need to do or know[0m
  - [1mFunctions via Hosting:[0m the app calls functions through Hosting at [38;2;177;185;249m/api/*[39m rather than the
    cloudfunctions.net address. It's a small change to the Firebase adapter, and it keeps the CSP
    free of a functions host.
  - [1mBusiness details:[0m the pages use placeholders in [38;2;177;185;249mapps/web/src/config/business.ts[39m for your
    registered name, address, phone, email and grievance officer. I didn't invent any. [38;2;177;185;249mpnpm [39m
    [38;2;177;185;249mlaunch:check[39m fails until they're filled in, and the live deploy runs it. The policy text is a
    draft and not legal advice, so have it reviewed.
  - [1mRefunds:[0m they're manual from the Razorpay dashboard, and the refund policy says so.
  - [1mDemo simulator:[0m the order simulator still moves paid orders to "delivered" on a timer, and the
    seed restaurants are fictional. [38;2;177;185;249mdocs/LAUNCH.md[39m says not to take real money until both are dealt
    with.
  - [1mStripe:[0m not bound yet. Create the three Stripe secrets and add them to [38;2;177;185;249msecrets.ts[39m when you want
    it.
  - [1mStyle CSP:[0m [38;2;177;185;249mstyle-src[39m keeps [38;2;177;185;249m'unsafe-inline'[39m because Razorpay and Stripe inject inline styles.
    Script rules stay strict.

